Bandit Level 14 - Level 15

Challenge: Submit the password for bandit14 to port 30000 on localhost to receive the password for the next level.

Solution

Read the password for bandit14:

cat /etc/bandit_pass/bandit14

Connect to port 30000 on localhost using nc:

nc localhost 30000

Paste the password into the connection and press Enter:



If the password is correct, the server responds with:

Correct!
BfMYroe26WYalil77FoDi9qh59eK5xNr

The second line is the password for bandit15.

Explanation
cat displays the current level's password.
nc localhost 30000 opens a TCP connection to port 30000 on the current machine.
Sending the correct password prompts the server to return the password for the next level.
What I learned
nc (Netcat) can connect to network services and send data.
localhost refers to the current machine you're logged into.
Some services require you to send input before they respond with data.
